On Thu, 2003-06-05 at 10:36, Mike Marsh wrote:
> I have tried reading the docs on aboot, and they left me very confused.  I
> am not very familiar with alphas, but I want to install gentoo on a DP264
> system I have.
> 
> I don't understand how to use and in what order to use "aboot.conf"
> "swriteboot".

The man page is helpful I believe I did:

1. Ensure that bootlx is in /boot. The file is a part of aboot.

2. swriteboot /dev/<boot partition> bootlx

   In your case: swriteboot /dev/sda bootlx.

3. Ensure that you have a valid aboot.conf file. I have located mine in
/boot/etc. 

Again check the man pages. The person writing this email is a 'orange
belt' with aboot. 

Stephen

